  "implementation": [
    "Rust shares the existing typed range-write planner and quota policy; no persisted filesystem shape changes.",
    "Aligned complete blocks without a destination hole reuse immutable source references, then update the existing destination inode once. Other ranges read a bounded span and reuse existing patch/hash/upload logic.",
    "Both descriptor owners and current read/write grants are checked. Native Python validates descriptor modes and append state, preserves explicit offsets and advances implicit cursors only after success.",
    "Copy calls may return short counts: at most 8 MiB aligned or 256 KiB otherwise. Zero/EOF calls publish nothing. Inode overlap is validated across the requested effective source interval before short-transfer limits, including aliases.",
    "Pinned pathlib discovers the native accelerator without modifying its source. ETXTBSY is supplied by the existing errno owner so actual accelerated-copy failures retain their source exception."
  ],
  "coverage": [
    "16 MiB varying-byte pathlib copy with complete SHA-256 readback and bounded root publications in real workerd/R2.",
    "Implicit and explicit offsets, partial-block overwrites, sparse gaps, EOF, negative arguments, overlap and file-size limits.",
    "Descriptor access modes and append rejection, retained unlinked source/destination inodes, current readonly denial, fresh Worker restoration and recreated-path isolation.",
    "Existing pathlib text, metadata, namespace, copied-tree, permission and restored-iterator/reader checks."
  ],
